@ [source_snapshot_uuid] df917e83-5c3d-43d6-9308-a79d65583699
@ [profile] cantor-sjs-staged-diff-acquisition/0.1

& [Requirements]
  + [SDA-001] strict request and receipt forms use closed profiles bounded fields and deny unknown machine fields
  + [SDA-002] request binds repository ID absolute repository root exact branch expected HEAD object format absolute Git executable expected raw SHA256 and limits
  + [SDA-003] executable bytes are SHA256 checked immediately before launch and again after final command
  + [SDA-004] child environment is cleared and only exact no-prompt no-lock no-lazy-fetch no-replacement no-system-config C-locale values are supplied
  + [SDA-005] exact read-only command vocabulary and flags forbid hooks external diff textconv submodule recursion mutation object write fetch and publication
  + [SDA-006] pre and post repository root branch HEAD object format must equal the request and each other
  + [SDA-007] exact absolute index path is resolved and raw bytes hash equal before and after all commands
  + [SDA-008] cached raw NUL-delimited records are strictly parsed with byte entry and aggregate bounds
  + [SDA-009] only A M D and R regular-file coordinates are accepted; all other status and mode shapes are refused
  + [SDA-010] raw baseline and staged blob bytes are read by exact object IDs and SHA256 hashed without treating repository object format as content identity
  + [SDA-011] explicit generated refresh paths are normalized unique exact M-coordinate subsets and cannot widen another status
  + [SDA-012] deterministic ordering and the published P0 digest function produce a valid existing DiffInventory
  + [SDA-013] receipt binds request executable version repository index inventory command count observation_only physical_contact true nonauthority and self-excluding digest
  + [SDA-014] CLI reads one bounded request file and emits receipt or inventory to stdout only with no repository or output-file mutation
  + [SDA-015] typed first-fault codes cover identity process parse object index bounds authority and replay failures
  + [SDA-016] tests cover valid add modify delete rename generated empty and deterministic replay plus every threat refusal family
  + [SDA-017] exact focused debug overflow-checked release workspace Clippy format evidence attribution commit and post-push gates pass
  + [SDA-018] commit-envelope change-set self-reference hook integration Git mutation provider activation and self-signature remain absent

& [Constraints]
  + C01 safe Rust only and no new Cargo dependency
  + C02 one absolute executable and repository root per request
  + C03 exact lowercase 40-hex expected HEAD for current SHA-1 repository profile
  + C04 object format is exactly sha1 for P1
  + C05 index path must be absolute regular file under resolved Git administrative root
  + C06 stdout stderr command count entry count path length blob bytes and aggregate bytes are bounded
  + C07 stderr must be empty on every successful Git command
  + C08 exit status must be zero
  + C09 path bytes must decode UTF-8 and normalize through P0 rules
  + C10 modes must be regular file 100644 or 100755 on every present side
  + C11 zero object IDs appear only on the absent side of add or delete
  + C12 rename score is required and bounded 0 through 100
  + C13 generated classifications are supplied data and exact-set validated
  + C14 inventory repository branch and predecessor equal the request
  + C15 observation receipt is not verification receipt or authority token
  + C16 no filesystem write by product code
  + C17 no ambient time randomness network provider model MCP or tool lookup
  + C18 no foreign unstaged or untracked path custody
  + C19 no live probe unless the exact local executable and repository identities match
  + C20 no claim that P1 resolves machine change-set self-inclusion

& [ImplementationBoundary]
  + one staged_diff_acquisition child module one read-only CLI unit integration/static tests fixtures builder evidence solution proof review narrative and publication bookend

& [SignatureState]
  + artifact lock proof review and satisfaction signature required before code
